WEBVTT

00:00:08,910 --> 00:00:15,150
I have searched for answers to the following question, but could I find any? So I'm asking you here.

00:00:16,430 --> 00:00:21,710
That's exactly what this is for. So I understand the function of black,

00:00:21,710 --> 00:00:30,030
sav, bloodroot, what it is used topically. But how does it work to help a cancer patient

00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:42,430
if it's used internally? So black, sav, bloodroot, understand is the name of a supplement. So the

00:00:42,430 --> 00:00:49,950
supplement that we have, that's called black, sav, bloodroot, maybe shouldn't be called that.

00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:57,150
Okay, well, why is it called that? Well, it does have, have a burdock root in it,

00:00:57,790 --> 00:01:04,830
grabiola powder, which is the leaf of the grabiola, chaperal, and it has bloodroot powder.

00:01:05,790 --> 00:01:16,910
So those four things are all known natural cancer killers. Bloodroot is an herb,

00:01:17,630 --> 00:01:23,550
so it doesn't grow here in Minnesota, but it grows in different parts of the world.

00:01:24,350 --> 00:01:30,190
I looked it up once, trying to look at how I could grow bloodroot. And I don't remember all the

00:01:30,190 --> 00:01:38,030
data that I found, but I gave up on trying to grow it myself. Burdock root grows everywhere. But

00:01:38,030 --> 00:01:45,150
I have enough burdock root, burdock plants, my 20 acre property to probably feed the world

00:01:47,070 --> 00:01:54,590
in cancer treatment. So burdock grows everywhere. It's a deep, deep rooted plant.

00:01:54,590 --> 00:02:02,430
Trying to pull a burdock plant out, and you will, you'd have to get the seventh

00:02:02,590 --> 00:02:10,830
regimen army to help you pull the thing out. The burdock roots go down, you know, 10, 15 feet

00:02:10,830 --> 00:02:16,030
into the soil. It's really, you have to really dig them out to get the root. Actually made some

00:02:16,030 --> 00:02:25,070
burdock root tincture last year, was it, or the year before, when we also had black wallets, we have

00:02:25,230 --> 00:02:32,110
black wallet tree. So we made black wallets, burdock root, something else of the tincture

00:02:33,230 --> 00:02:41,230
mulled. I think I had, because we grow mulled, and I can't remember something else. But burdock

00:02:41,230 --> 00:02:48,030
root is known as a great cancer killer. Graviola is sour sap, and it's the leaf of the

00:02:48,110 --> 00:02:54,910
Graviola plant that's a great cancer killer itself. And chaperale is another cancer killer.

00:02:55,630 --> 00:03:04,990
The chaperale, I believe, is an seacte, as well as an hoxy. So those are just four great natural

00:03:04,990 --> 00:03:16,510
cancer-killing herbs. Now, black sap, topical, is actually made from blood root. So it's basically

00:03:16,510 --> 00:03:24,510
dried blood root that is made into a sap with some sort of emulsifier, and then you put that on

00:03:24,510 --> 00:03:34,590
topically to kill melanoma and other skin cancers. It could be really good for it as a topical.

00:03:35,710 --> 00:03:41,630
I know people who have actually taken the black sap, orally, I think it's a waste of money because

00:03:41,710 --> 00:03:48,510
black sap itself is expensive to buy it, made up as a sap, and you could get the powdered blood

00:03:48,510 --> 00:03:57,230
root for pennies of the dollar to what you're paying for the black sap. So that's not a smart way to

00:03:57,230 --> 00:04:05,710
take it. But the black sap blood root capsules that you're talking about here are not just blood

00:04:06,110 --> 00:04:12,350
root, and it's not sap. So I don't know why they named it that. It's just the company named it that.

00:04:12,830 --> 00:04:20,110
This company also makes black sap that I recommend the black sap with the MSO for people with

00:04:20,110 --> 00:04:26,990
topical cancers, and maybe they did it just to help people understand that this is a topic,

00:04:26,990 --> 00:04:34,030
this is an oral quote-unquote black sap, well, it's not a sap, and it's not only blood root,

00:04:34,030 --> 00:04:41,630
but that's just what they named it.

